From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: accept the cpuset_v2_mode mount option

Android mounts the cpuset hierarchy with

  mount("none", "/dev/cpuset", "cgroup", ..., "cpuset,noprefix,cpuset_v2_mode")

(system/core/libprocessgroup/setup/cgroup_map_write.cpp). 3.10 takes any
option it does not know for a controller name and fails the mount with
ENOENT, so /dev/cpuset would stay empty even with CONFIG_CPUSETS enabled
("libprocessgroup: Failed to mount controller cpuset: No such file or
directory").

Parse the option into a new root flag, CGRP_ROOT_CPUSET_V2_MODE, and show
it in /proc/mounts. The flag is for the cpuset controller; nothing reads
it yet, the next patch does.

What userspace asks for with this option is that a cpuset gets its CPUs
back after they were offline. "cpuset: restore the requested CPUs when
they come back online" already does that for every cpuset hierarchy,
whatever its mount options.

Derived from upstream:
  e1cba4b85daa "cgroup: Add mount flag to enable cpuset to use v2 behavior
               in v1 cgroup" (v4.14)

Adapted for 3.10:
- The flag is bit 3 of the root flags (bit 16 upstream; 3.10 uses bits
  0-2 and has no room reserved).
- Like the other root flags it takes part in the "new mount options do
  not match the existing superblock" comparison and cannot be changed by
  a remount.

Compile-tested as part of the cpuset series with CONFIG_CPUSETS=y: full
zImage with the GCC 4.9 arm-linux-androideabi prebuilt, and
kernel/cpuset.o and kernel/cgroup.o at every step of the series; no
warnings in the files touched. Not run on the device.

[combined set, 2026-11-06] Header only, the diff is the staged one. The
paragraph above said "five patches". The series was staged as five
(staging/backport-cpusets 0014-0018) and compiled step by step in that
form; the combined set has four of them, 0015-0018. The fifth, "cpuset:
let CAP_SYS_NICE move other users' tasks into a cpuset" (staged 0015),
is replaced by "cgroup: one credential rule for moving another user's
task" (0014). The four were compiled again in that form, as one zImage
build of the whole combined series, not step by step.
---
 include/linux/cgroup.h | 6 ++++++
 kernel/cgroup.c        | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/cgroup.h b/include/linux/cgroup.h
index 32a4f95..d860a96 100644
--- a/include/linux/cgroup.h
+++ b/include/linux/cgroup.h
@@ -281,6 +281,12 @@ enum {
 
 	CGRP_ROOT_NOPREFIX	= (1 << 1), /* mounted subsystems have no named prefix */
 	CGRP_ROOT_XATTR		= (1 << 2), /* supports extended attributes */
+
+	/*
+	 * "cpuset_v2_mode" mount option: the cpusets of this hierarchy handle
+	 * CPU hotplug the way cgroup v2 does.  Read by kernel/cpuset.c only.
+	 */
+	CGRP_ROOT_CPUSET_V2_MODE = (1 << 3),
 };
 
 /*
diff --git a/kernel/cgroup.c b/kernel/cgroup.c
index 9f0fb7e..5649666 100644
--- a/kernel/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup.c
@@ -1098,6 +1098,8 @@ static int cgroup_show_options(struct seq_file *seq, struct dentry *dentry)
 		seq_puts(seq, ",noprefix");
 	if (root->flags & CGRP_ROOT_XATTR)
 		seq_puts(seq, ",xattr");
+	if (root->flags & CGRP_ROOT_CPUSET_V2_MODE)
+		seq_puts(seq, ",cpuset_v2_mode");
 	if (strlen(root->release_agent_path))
 		seq_printf(seq, ",release_agent=%s", root->release_agent_path);
 	if (test_bit(CGRP_CPUSET_CLONE_CHILDREN, &root->top_cgroup.flags))
@@ -1174,6 +1176,10 @@ static int parse_cgroupfs_options(char *data, struct cgroup_sb_opts *opts)
 			opts->flags |= CGRP_ROOT_XATTR;
 			continue;
 		}
+		if (!strcmp(token, "cpuset_v2_mode")) {
+			opts->flags |= CGRP_ROOT_CPUSET_V2_MODE;
+			continue;
+		}
 		if (!strncmp(token, "release_agent=", 14)) {
 			/* Specifying two release agents is forbidden */
 			if (opts->release_agent)
